    "message": "Reduce repeated CI test work and rebalance active shards\n\nRetain every lane, ID-order, fresh-cache and warm-cache comparison while counting entered files in the existing warm replay and comparing equal token streams by columns. Add negative controls for the comparisons and record accounting.\n\nMatch production allocation-limit snapshots and commit policy for sanitizer in-process driver commands, restoring the caller policy after every command. Preserve plain tests' allocation policy and verify stale snapshots against fresh-child results.\n\nRegenerate all five active cost tables from sixty logs of three passing merge candidates with the unchanged cost collector. Keep all 167 headings, four shards, CPU grants, O3 settings and detectors. Record logs, provenance, held-out predictions and reproduction in buster-performance/docs/measurements/ci-work-reuse-2658-2026-11-26.\n\nPart of #2658. Original agent-authored code and documentation; generated cost data comes only from this repository's CI logs.\n\nAgent session: 6b07eee5-9a58-83ed-88f1-9e324a97a063 (OpenAI session ID; no share URL is exposed)\nModel: OpenAI / GPT-6 Astra Pro\n\nSigned-off-by: David Gonzalez Martin <davidgmbb@gmail.com>",
